,y(0)=y(5)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions $y(0)=y(5)=0$ yields the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Since the zero solution is not an eigenfunction, $\\lambda =0$ does not correspond to an eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+16\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 4\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $A=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(5)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nB\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n20\\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{400}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "472cbb79-e22b-50d2-a997-93130ff66c22" :knowledge-point/title "Trigonometric Eigenfunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c02d751b-6dc1-58c4-9827-6697a10da147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374668} {:answer/id #uuid "cc981746-8442-5899-8593-7c7c903d75bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374669} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9aa9f6-fb77-5dfb-996b-596371ddd2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374670} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd88f65-fed7-50d4-84ef-a2424db35326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9aa9f6-fb77-5dfb-996b-596371ddd2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374670} :answer-field/id #uuid "2189c44e-c6fc-5459-91e4-e02ae31ddba1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abd0e83e-9292-52a1-923d-656568a129ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374673} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4dfd05-1105-50fd-abb0-0f2061527683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374674} {:answer/id #uuid "65dc78d1-78c5-5a8f-9dfa-cfcde797c39d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374675} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9e